{%- comment -%}
  hreflang-crawlable-links.liquid

  Why this exists: Shopify's native localization switcher (snippets/localization-form.liquid)
  is a <select> + POST form, not real <a href> hyperlinks. Search-engine crawlers (and Ahrefs'
  Site Audit) cannot follow a form submit, so every /de/* and /en/* page on this store is only
  discoverable via the XML sitemap + <link rel="alternate" hreflang> tags, never via an actual
  crawled internal link. This is the confirmed root cause of thousands of "orphan page (no
  incoming internal links)" flags in the live Ahrefs crawl (see audit-results/*.md) — hreflang
  tags let Google find the pages, but pass zero internal link equity, and link-graph-based tools
  flag them as orphaned.

  Fix: render one real, crawlable <a href> per available language, pointing to the CURRENT
  page's equivalent path in that locale (same URL-building logic as hreflang-tags.liquid, kept
  in sync intentionally). Visually hidden (not display:none, so it stays crawlable/accessible to
  screen readers) — this changes zero visible UI/UX. It is additive only: the visible <select>
  language switcher is untouched.

  Safe by construction:
  - No visual change (visually-hidden, not display:none/aria-hidden).
  - Does not touch header, footer, cart, checkout, variant picker, or any existing markup.
  - Reuses the same request.path + localization.language.root_url math already proven correct
    in hreflang-tags.liquid, so URLs match what's already emitted in <head>.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if localization.available_languages.size > 1 -%}
  <nav class="visually-hidden" aria-label="{{ 'content.language' | t | default: 'Language' }}" data-hreflang-crawlable-links>
    {%- for language in localization.available_languages -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign language_path = request.path
        if localization.language.root_url != '/'
          assign language_path = request.path | remove_first: localization.language.root_url
        endif
        if language_path == blank
          assign language_path = '/'
        endif
        if language.root_url == '/'
          assign language_url = request.origin | append: language_path
        elsif language_path == '/'
          assign language_url = request.origin | append: language.root_url
        else
          assign locale_suffix = language_path | remove_first: '/'
          assign language_root = language.root_url
          assign language_root_last = language_root | slice: -1, 1
          if language_root_last == '/'
            assign language_url = request.origin | append: language_root | append: locale_suffix
          else
            assign language_url = request.origin | append: language_root | append: '/' | append: locale_suffix
          endif
        endif
        if language_url contains '?'
          assign language_url = language_url | split: '?' | first
        endif
      -%}
      <a href="{{ language_url }}" hreflang="{{ language.iso_code }}" tabindex="-1">{{ language.endonym_name | capitalize }}</a>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </nav>
{%- endif -%}
